Q: How to Routes URL Dynamic with Switch Case? A: <p>&lt;?php</p>
<p>session_start();</p>
<p>require 'database.php'; // Provides the $pdo connection</p>
<p>$error = '';</p>
<p>$username = '';</p>
<p>if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] === 'POST') {</p>
<pre><code>$username = trim($\_POST\['username'\] ?? '');

$password = $\_POST\['password'\] ?? '';

if ($username === '' || $password === '') {

    $error = 'Bitte Benutzername und Passwort eingeben.';

} else {

    $stmt = $pdo-\&gt;prepare('SELECT id, benutzername, passwort, ist_admin FROM benutzer WHERE benutzername = ?');

    $stmt-\&gt;execute(\[$username\]);

    $user = $stmt-\&gt;fetch();

    if ($user &amp;&amp; password_verify($password, $user\['passwort'\])) {

        $\_SESSION\['user_id'\]     = $user\['id'\];

        $\_SESSION\['benutzername'\] = $user\['benutzername'\];

        $\_SESSION\['ist_admin'\]    = $user\['ist_admin'\];

        header('Location: index.php?view=products');

        exit;

    } else {

        // Generische Meldung aus Sicherheitsgründen (nicht verraten, ob Username oder Passwort falsch war)

        $error = 'Benutzername oder Passwort ist falsch.';

    }

}
</code></pre>
<p>}</p>
<p>// View wird gerendert</p>
<p>require 'views/login_view.php';</p>
<p>&lt;?php require 'includes/header.php'; ?&gt;</p>
<p>&lt;!-- Fehlermeldung anzeigen --&gt;</p>
<p>&lt;?php if (!empty($error)): ?&gt;</p>
<pre><code>\&lt;div class=&quot;alert alert-danger&quot;\&gt;\&lt;?= htmlspecialchars($error) ?\&gt;\&lt;/div\&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>&lt;?php endif; ?&gt;</p>
<p>&lt;form method=&quot;post&quot; style=&quot;max-width:400px;&quot;&gt;</p>
<pre><code>\&lt;div class=&quot;mb-3&quot;\&gt;

    \&lt;label class=&quot;form-label&quot;\&gt;Benutzername\&lt;/label\&gt;

    \&lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; name=&quot;username&quot; class=&quot;form-control&quot; value=&quot;\&lt;?= htmlspecialchars($username ?? '') ?\&gt;&quot; required\&gt;

\&lt;/div\&gt;

\&lt;div class=&quot;mb-3&quot;\&gt;

    \&lt;label class=&quot;form-label&quot;\&gt;Passwort\&lt;/label\&gt;

    \&lt;input type=&quot;password&quot; name=&quot;password&quot; class=&quot;form-control&quot; required\&gt;

\&lt;/div\&gt;

\&lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot;\&gt;Login\&lt;/button\&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>&lt;/form&gt;</p>
<p>&lt;div class=&quot;mt-3&quot;&gt;</p>
<pre><code>\&lt;p\&gt;Noch kein Konto? \&lt;a href=&quot;index.php?view=register&quot;\&gt;Hier registrieren\&lt;/a\&gt;.\&lt;/p\&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>&lt;/div&gt;</p>
<p>&lt;?php require 'includes/footer.php'; ?&gt;</p>

Q: How to change the position of a gif? A: <p>For positioning to work, the PARENT element  also needs their position property to be set <strong>explicitly</strong>. Even if it's just <code>position: relative;</code></p>
<p>So try this:</p>
<pre><code>.magpie {
position: relative;
}

.magpie img {
display: block;
position: relative;
left: -50px;
}
</code></pre>
